<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Eburones</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 53 BCE (approx.) · capital Atuatuca</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Belgic people between the Meuse and the Rhine who destroyed a Roman legion in 54 BCE and were wiped out by Caesar in revenge.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Eburones lived between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, in modern eastern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-belgium">Belgium</a> and the southern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Caesar</a> counts them among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germani-cisrhenani">Germani Cisrhenani</a> and says they had paid tribute to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aduatuci">Aduatuci</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They were ruled jointly by two kings, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambiorix">Ambiorix</a> and the elderly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catuvolcus">Catuvolcus</a>. Their stronghold was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atuatuca">Atuatuca</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Caesar</a> stationed troops for the winter of 54 BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 54 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambiorix">Ambiorix</a> lured the legion and a half under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintus-titurius-sabinus">Sabinus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-aurunculeius-cotta">Cotta</a> out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atuatuca">Atuatuca</a> and destroyed it. In 53 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Caesar</a> invited neighbouring peoples to plunder their land; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catuvolcus">Catuvolcus</a> poisoned himself with yew, while Ambiorix escaped. Their territory was later settled by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tungri">Tungri</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/eburones.jpg" alt="Eburones" width="320" height="427"><figcaption>Image: ArtMechanic · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ambiorix.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 53 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Atuatuca</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ambiorix, Catuvolcus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/belgium">Belgium</a>, <a href="/countries/netherlands">Netherlands</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=eburones" aria-label="Eburones on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4795 423 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Eburones lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5115 679h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5115 679h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Belgium. <a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=eburones">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

